            <title>[LU-20820] conf-sanity test_133: lctl pool_add OST[0-14] silently skips OSTs 0010-0014</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20820</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_133 fails:&lt;br/&gt;
  failed to add OST&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0-14&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; to the pool&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;'lctl pool_add lustre.testpool OST&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0-14&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;' (poolostrange = OSTCOUNT - 2 = 14 with the 16 OSTs this cluster has) returned:&lt;br/&gt;
  pool_add: lustre-OST0010_UUID is not part of the 'lustre' fs.&lt;br/&gt;
  pool_add: lustre-OST0011_UUID is not part of the 'lustre' fs.&lt;br/&gt;
  pool_add: lustre-OST0012_UUID is not part of the 'lustre' fs.&lt;br/&gt;
  pool_add: lustre-OST0013_UUID is not part of the 'lustre' fs.&lt;br/&gt;
  pool_add: lustre-OST0014_UUID is not part of the 'lustre' fs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lctl expanded the decimal range &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0-14&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; to the literal zero-padded strings 0000..0014 instead of converting decimal indices 10-14 to their hex OST names (000a-000e). The real OSTs are named OST0000-OST000f (16 OSTs, hex), so OST0010-OST0014 do not exist and pool_add reports them as not part of the fs, failing the test. test_133 only requires OSTCOUNT &amp;gt;= 4 and has presumably always run with fewer than 10 OSTs in ordinary CI, never exercising a two-digit range.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not this patch's: the diff under review does not touch conf-sanity.sh's test_133 or create_pool(), and it makes no change to lctl's pool_add range parsing; it is limited to test-framework.sh/functions.sh node-list helpers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/12b03951-22b4-42bd-bca0-7b0147c3eafc" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/12b03951-22b4-42bd-bca0-7b0147c3eafc&lt;/a&gt; (test_133)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-51976-ps6-684d26660414 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/51976" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/51976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
